    "Hypertension management after transplantation aims to prevent organ damage with specific BP targets restricting <160/90 mm Hg to avoid graft thrombosis. CCBs are preferred for their positive effects on GFR. RAS inhibitors may be used in patients with certain comorbidities post-transplantation. In stroke, BP management involves consideration of stroke type and therapeutic objectives. Recommendations vary for acute ICH management with different interventions for SBP >220 mm Hg.": "",
